**54.** In relation to a DATE “order date”, a BOOLEAN “adopter a citizen”, a BOOLEAN “habitually resident” and a BOOLEAN “later ceased”, a United Kingdom adoption order on means AdoptionCase where the adopted person a minor on the date of the order or adoption is TRUE, the adopted person already a British citizen is FALSE, an order of a court in the United Kingdom authorising the adoption is TRUE, an order of a court in a qualifying territory authorising the adoption is FALSE, a Convention adoption effected under the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom is FALSE, date of the order or Convention adoption is order date, the adopter or, in a joint adoption, one of the adopters a British citizen on that date is adopter a citizen, the adopter or, in a joint adoption, both of the adopters habitually resident in the United Kingdom or a designated territory on that date is habitually resident and the order or Convention adoption since ceased to have effect, whether on annulment or otherwise is later ceased.

<!-- l4: decide:a Convention adoption on -->

**55.** In relation to a DATE “adoption date”, a BOOLEAN “adopter a citizen” and a BOOLEAN “habitually resident”, a Convention adoption on means AdoptionCase where the adopted person a minor on the date of the order or adoption is TRUE, the adopted person already a British citizen is FALSE, an order of a court in the United Kingdom authorising the adoption is FALSE, an order of a court in a qualifying territory authorising the adoption is FALSE, a Convention adoption effected under the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom is TRUE, date of the order or Convention adoption is adoption date, the adopter or, in a joint adoption, one of the adopters a British citizen on that date is adopter a citizen, the adopter or, in a joint adoption, both of the adopters habitually resident in the United Kingdom or a designated territory on that date is habitually resident and the order or Convention adoption since ceased to have effect, whether on annulment or otherwise is FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:a Gibraltar adoption order case -->

**56.** A Gibraltar adoption order case means AdoptionCase where the adopted person a minor on the date of the order or adoption is TRUE, the adopted person already a British citizen is FALSE, an order of a court in the United Kingdom authorising the adoption is FALSE, an order of a court in a qualifying territory authorising the adoption is TRUE, a Convention adoption effected under the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom is FALSE, date of the order or Convention adoption is YMD with 2005, 4 and 1, the adopter or, in a joint adoption, one of the adopters a British citizen on that date is TRUE, the adopter or, in a joint adoption, both of the adopters habitually resident in the United Kingdom or a designated territory on that date is FALSE and the order or Convention adoption since ceased to have effect, whether on annulment or otherwise is FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:a pre-appointed-day Gibraltar order case -->

**57.** A pre-appointed-day Gibraltar order case means AdoptionCase where the adopted person a minor on the date of the order or adoption is TRUE, the adopted person already a British citizen is FALSE, an order of a court in the United Kingdom authorising the adoption is FALSE, an order of a court in a qualifying territory authorising the adoption is TRUE, a Convention adoption effected under the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom is FALSE, date of the order or Convention adoption is YMD with 2001, 4 and 1, the adopter or, in a joint adoption, one of the adopters a British citizen on that date is TRUE, the adopter or, in a joint adoption, both of the adopters habitually resident in the United Kingdom or a designated territory on that date is FALSE and the order or Convention adoption since ceased to have effect, whether on annulment or otherwise is FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:an adoption of a person already a British citizen -->

**58.** An adoption of a person already a British citizen means AdoptionCase where the adopted person a minor on the date of the order or adoption is TRUE, the adopted person already a British citizen is TRUE, an order of a court in the United Kingdom authorising the adoption is TRUE, an order of a court in a qualifying territory authorising the adoption is FALSE, a Convention adoption effected under the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom is FALSE, date of the order or Convention adoption is YMD with 2010, 9 and 15, the adopter or, in a joint adoption, one of the adopters a British citizen on that date is TRUE, the adopter or, in a joint adoption, both of the adopters habitually resident in the United Kingdom or a designated territory on that date is TRUE and the order or Convention adoption since ceased to have effect, whether on annulment or otherwise is FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:the foundling -->

**59.** The foundling means a foundling found on with YMD with 2020, 6 and 1, TRUE and FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:the rebutted foundling -->

**60.** The rebutted foundling means a foundling found on with YMD with 2020, 6 and 1, TRUE and TRUE.

<!-- l4: decide:the forces child -->

**61.** The forces child means a child born in the United Kingdom on with YMD with 2015, 6 and 1, FALSE, FALSE and TRUE.

<!-- l4: decide:the child of visitors -->

**62.** The child of visitors means a child of visitors born on with YMD with 2012, 5 and 10, TRUE, FALSE and TRUE.

<!-- l4: decide:the ten-year lead case -->

**63.** The ten-year lead case means a ten-year applicant born on with YMD with 1995, 3 and 1, 90, TRUE, FALSE and TRUE.

<!-- l4: decide:the applicant of bad character -->

**64.** The applicant of bad character means a ten-year applicant born on with YMD with 1995, 3 and 1, 90, TRUE, FALSE and FALSE.

